hey everyone this is Lucy I'm a  Solutions architect working at AWS and  in this video I'm going to be explaining  to you why you should not become a  Solutions architect all right let me  take a step back and explain why when  you first come across the world of cloud  computing you probably started to see  the phrase Solutions Architects thrown  around everywhere people talk about how  the solutions Arctic job pays a lot of  money and you get to work with cool  technology every day there's even two  AWS certifications named after the  solutions architect title but this role  isn't for everyone not everyone should  become an AWS Solutions architect and no  I'm not saying that you don't have what  it takes to become an AWS Solutions  architect I truly believe that anyone  can become whatever they want as long as  they set their mind to achieving it what  I'm saying is it's important for you to  find a career that aligns with your  personality your interests and what you  find fulfilling what a lot of people  don't understand about the solutions  architect role is that just like every  other role it comes with a lot of things  you may enjoy but also a lot of things  that make you want to pull your hair out  and of course how much you end up liking  the role all depends on who you are as a  person I'm going to be sharing five  reasons you should not become a  Solutions architect and at the end of  this video I'd encourage all of you to  comment below whether you still like to  become a Solutions architect or maybe  consider a different career path this  video is honestly not me trying to  convince you not to become a Solutions  architect I just want to provide you  with the transparency of what it's  actually like working in this kind of  role if 99 of you in the comments say  you still want to become a Solutions  architect that's really great but if I  can help the other one percent realize  that this role isn't actually what they  expected it to be then I hope some  people save some time and money in their  career with all that being said let's  jump straight into it reason number one  you should not become an AWS Solutions  architect if you don't enjoy interacting  with customers this is a big one as a  Solutions architect I spend almost every  day talking to customers whether that's  meeting them over a video call or  sending emails back and forth it's quite  rare for me to have many days in a row  where I just sit in front of my laptop  all day and do my work without talking  to anyone the main responsibility of an  AWS Solutions architect is to be a  trusted technical advisor for companies  looking to build things in the cloud so  if you're someone who doesn't like the  idea of spending the next three to five  years of your career working directly  with customers then this role is not for  you reason number two you should not  become an AWS Solutions architect if  you're not willing to continuously learn  and build new skills at AWS all  solutions Architects have one thing in  common we all have to sharpen the saw  this is a term we use internally at AWS  to describe the time we spend improving  our technical skills and keeping up to  date with the latest technology Trends  the cloud industry is constantly  evolving and in order to provide the  best architectural guidance to our  customers you're expected to learn new  things every week this could involve  getting AWS certifications catching up  with the latest product updates or  diving deeper into a technical area  you're interested in for example  containers or machine learning in order  to succeed in this field in the long run  you'll need to have the willingness to  proactively develop your technical  skills so if this doesn't sound appear  to you maybe it's best to consider a  different career path  quick pause this video is brought to you  by skillshare skillshare is an online  learning community with thousands of  inspiring classes for anyone who loves  learning and wants to explore their  creativity and learn new skills from  Tech and finance to productivity graphic  design and more you can find classes  that will match with your goals and  interests here is a Class by hashtag  learning providing an absolute  beginner's introduction to Amazon web  services if you're at the start of your  Cloud Learning Journey I would recommend  checking out the class I joined  skillshare to learn more about tech and  productivity and by taking classes like  these I hope to continue building my  skills the first 1000 people to use the  link in the video description below will  get a free one month trial of skillshare  so thank you skillshare for sponsoring  today's video reason number three you  should not become an AWS Solutions  Architects if you want to make a direct  impact now as I've mentioned earlier  Solutions Architects are pretty much  technical advisors for the customer we  provide advice and suggestions on what  customers should build on the cloud and  how they should build it but it's up to  them to do the actual implementation  unlike about architects who can actually  build things out for the customer  Solutions Architects are a lot more  hands-off and at AWS we're actually not  allowed to go into the customer's  account and build anything out for them  it's up to the customer to either do it  themselves or hire someone else for  example a cloud architect so if you  prefer being more Hands-On when working  with customers I would recommend looking  into the cloud Arctic role reason number  four you should not become an AWS  Solutions architect if you want your  role to be very clearly defined this is  a role where you need to learn how to  navigate ambiguity we're not given a  piece of paper that tells us exactly  what we should be doing every single day  so it's our responsibility to figure out  how to juggle our customer work our  internal projects and other commitments  we do have broader essay goals to aim  for as a team but it's up to us to  figure out how to achieve them which is  exciting but at the same time a little  bit intimidating so as a Solutions  architect you'll need to be comfortable  with being uncomfortable I definitely  think this is something you can get used  to over time but if you want a job with  a clearly defined set of  responsibilities then it might be good  to look for a role with less ambiguity  and reason number five is you should not  become an AWS Solutions architect if you  find something else a lot more  fulfilling alright so I recently read a  book that introduces the concept of  ikigai and this is a Japanese term that  Loosely translates to reason for being  according to this book you can use this  as a guide to find your true purpose in  life this can also be applied to your  career essentially an ideal career is  where you get to do what you love do  what you're good at do what the world  needs and do what you can be paid for  I'd recommend spending some time at the  end of this video to try and discover  your own ikigai it might not put you to  an exact job but it will definitely help  you get more clarity on what you value  in the career alright thank you so much  for sticking until the end of this video  please remember to give this video a  like if you got something out of it and  comment below whether you'd still like  to become a Solutions architect alright  bye for now
 

